</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-09-22.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="185041"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#185041" label="[18:50:41]">&lt;andydude&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I worked on my hex0 implementation</span></div><div class="line" id="185456"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#185456" label="[18:54:56]">&lt;andydude&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> <a rel="nofollow" href="https://gist.github.com/andydude/7ba3c7444f4f666bc5a8d713e6cc0e73">https://gist.github.com/andydude/7ba3c7444f4f666bc5a8d713e6cc0e73</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="225805"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#225805" label="[22:58:05]">&lt;nimaje&gt;</a></span><span class="message">using COM for comment seems strange and confusing, do you have to save characters for some reason? I would use a generator function instead of what you are doing with dfauto and reduce, takes some time to understand the way you have written it (or maybe itertools.accumulate if you want). Not sure why you merge tokens via pdauto and reduce only to later drop everything that isn't hex digits</span></div><div class="line" id="225807"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#225807" label="[22:58:07]">&lt;nimaje&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and isn't that code broken if someone uses odd groupings of digits?</span></div><div class="line" id="232813"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#232813" label="[23:28:13]">&lt;nimaje&gt;</a></span><span class="message">And I don't see why you need that SOF state (start of file?) you could start with WS (whitespace?)</span></div><br /></div></body></html>